{%- doc -%}
  Letter swap label (rewrite of the supplied letterswap example): on hover or keyboard focus of
  the enclosing link/button, each letter slides up and an identical copy follows from below,
  one after another. Pure CSS (effects.css); screen readers read the plain text.

  Both visible copies of each letter are drawn by CSS from data-c, so the label exists once in
  the HTML and link text reads "Shop", not "ShopSShhoopp", to search engines.

  @param {string} text - Label text (plain, unescaped)
  @param {string} [from] - Stagger origin: start (default) or center

  @example
  {% render 'letter-swap', text: block.settings.label_1 %}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign letters = text | split: ''
  assign mid = letters.size | minus: 1 | divided_by: 2
-%}
<span class="ls"><span class="visually-hidden">{{ text | escape }}</span><span class="ls__row" aria-hidden="true">
  {%- for letter in letters -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign i = forloop.index0
      if from == 'center'
        assign i = forloop.index0 | minus: mid | abs
      endif
    -%}
    <span class="ls__c" style="--i: {{ i }}" data-c="{% if letter == ' ' %}&nbsp;{% else %}{{ letter | escape }}{% endif %}"></span>
  {%- endfor -%}
</span></span>
